@inject PlanGate Gate
@inject Localizer Loc

@* A crown marking something the current plan doesn't include, and the way into the plan comparison.

   Renders NOTHING unless the feature is actually out of reach — so a Pro (or beta-cohort "unlimited") account
   never sees a crown anywhere, and the app doesn't nag people who already have everything. That also means these
   can be scattered liberally at Pro entry points without turning the UI into an advert for most users.

   Clicking goes through PlanGate.Require, the same call the real gates use: it re-checks entitlement and raises
   the single upgrade prompt. No separate "show the modal" path exists, so the crown can never disagree with the
   gate it decorates. *@

@if (!Gate.Allows(Feature))
{
    @if (Static)
    {
        @* For use INSIDE an existing clickable element whose own handler already gates (the Trends chip, Import,
           Add account…). A <button> nested in a <button> is invalid HTML and browsers recover from it by
           splitting the markup, so the crown has to be inert there — the host's click raises the prompt. *@
        <span class="pro-lock pro-lock-static" title="@Loc["Part of Pro — see what’s included"]">
            <Icon Name="crown" Class="pro-lock-crown" />
        </span>
    }
    else
    {
        <button type="button"
                class="pro-lock @(Bar ? "pro-lock-bar" : "")"
                title="@Loc["Part of Pro — see what’s included"]"
                aria-label="@Loc["Part of Pro — see what’s included"]"
                @onclick="Open" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <Icon Name="crown" Class="pro-lock-crown" />
            @if (Bar)
            {
                <span class="pro-lock-txt">@(Label ?? Loc["Part of Pro"])</span>
                <span class="pro-lock-go" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
            }
        </button>
    }
}

@code {
    /// <summary>A <see cref="FinApp.Contracts.PlanFeatures"/> key.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Feature { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>Full-width bar (standing in for content that has been withheld) rather than an inline chip
    /// (marking a control that is still visible).</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Bar { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Overrides the bar's wording. Ignored for the inline chip, which is crown-only.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Render an inert span instead of a button, for placing inside a control that already gates.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Static { get; set; }

    private void Open() => Gate.Require(Feature);
}
